.RI "class \fBAtomicLock\fP"
.br
.RI "A minimal user‑mode spin lock based on an atomic integer\&. The lock stores the managed thread ID of the owning thread\&. A value of \fR0\fP means the lock is free\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBBarrier\fP"
.br
.RI "A user‑mode barrier that synchronizes multiple threads across repeated phases\&. The barrier waits until a specified number of threads have arrived, then opens and allows all participants to continue\&. After the phase completes, the barrier resets and becomes ready for the next cycle\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBBarrierNewPhaseLockException\fP"
.br
.RI "Exception thrown when a barrier phase transition fails due to an invalid lock state or an inconsistent phase update\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBByteIndex\fP"
.br
.RI "Represents a thread-safe index counter that can be incremented, decremented, and compared atomically\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBEpoch\fP"
.br
.RI "Represents a lightweight Read-Copy-Update (RCU) epoch counter used to track active reader sections\&. Each call to \fBAssign\fP enters a reader epoch, and each call to \fBLeave\fP exits it\&. Writers may only proceed when the epoch value indicates that no readers are active\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBEventGroup< TFastType >\fP"
.br
.RI "Represents a lightweight event group based on a fast bit‑storage type\&. \fBEventGroup<TFastType>\fP allows individual bit positions to be set, cleared, flipped, queried, or waited on\&. The underlying bit container is provided by \fITFastType\fP , which must implement \fBIFastType\fP\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "interface \fBILock\fP"
.br
.RI "Defines the minimal contract for a synchronization primitive capable of providing mutual exclusion\&. Implementations of \fBILock\fP may wrap lightweight in‑process mechanisms (such as Monitor) or heavier inter‑process constructs (such as Mutex)\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "interface \fBILock< T >\fP"
.br
.RI "Extends \fBILock\fP by exposing the underlying synchronization handle\&. This is useful for advanced scenarios where the caller may need direct access to the wrapped primitive (e\&.g\&., Mutex, Monitor object)\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "interface \fBILockedObject< T >\fP"
.br
.RI "Defines a minimal lock‑protected value container interface\&. Implementations provide controlled read and write access to a value of type \fIT\fP  using a caller‑supplied synchronization mechanism\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "interface \fBILockFreeQueue< T >\fP"
.br
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBIndex\fP"
.br
.RI "Represents a thread-safe index counter that can be incremented, decremented, and compared atomically\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "interface \fBISpinlock< T >\fP"
.br
.RI "Extends \fBILock<T>\fP with spin‑lock‑specific diagnostics and metadata\&. Implementations of \fBISpinlock<T>\fP represent busy‑wait mutual exclusion primitives where threads repeatedly attempt to acquire the lock without yielding\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBLightConditionVariable\fP"
.br
.RI "A lightweight and minimal condition variable designed for simple thread synchronization scenarios\&. Unlike the heavy and business‑oriented primitives in \&.NET, \fBLightConditionVariable\fP provides a straightforward FIFO wait‑list and wake‑up mechanism suitable for most everyday use cases\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBLightCountingSpinlock< T >\fP"
.br
.RI "Implements a counting spinlock, a non‑blocking synchronization primitive that allows a bounded number of threads to enter a critical section concurrently\&. Unlike traditional binary spinlocks, which permit only a single thread at a time, a counting spinlock maintains an atomic counter representing the current available capacity\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBLightFutex\fP"
.br
.RI "Provides a lightweight reentrant futex-like synchronization primitive\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBLightLatch\fP"
.br
.RI "A one-shot countdown synchronization primitive\&. The latch starts in the locked state and releases all waiting threads once its internal counter reaches zero\&. After releasing, the latch remains permanently open\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBLightLock\fP"
.br
.RI "Provides a minimal wrapper around Monitor to offer lightweight mutual exclusion\&. \fBLightLock\fP is intended for short, low‑overhead critical sections where a full synchronization primitive would be unnecessary\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBLightMMQueue< T >\fP"
.br
.RI "A bounded lock‑free multi‑producer, multi‑consumer (MPMC) queue\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBLightMutex< T >\fP"
.br
.RI "A lightweight non‑blocking mutex built on top of \fBLightCountingSpinlock<T>\fP\&. This mutex provides binary spinlock semantics (capacity 1) combined with strict owner‑tracking to ensure that only the thread which successfully acquired the lock may access the protected value or release the lock\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBLightSaveQueueEntry< T >\fP"
.br
.RI "Represents a single slot inside a lock‑free LightQueue\&. Each entry stores a sequence number used for producer/consumer coordination, and an optional value of type \fIT\fP \&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBLightSpinlock< T >\fP"
.br
.RI "Provides a lightweight atomic spinlock that protects a single value\&. \fBLightSpinlock<T>\fP uses pure atomic operations and busy‑wait acquisition, making it suitable for extremely short critical sections\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBLightThread\fP"
.br
.RI "A lightweight and minimal thread implementation designed for simple and common synchronization scenarios\&. Unlike the complex and business-oriented threading abstractions in \&.NET, \fBLightThread\fP provides a straightforward wait-and-wake mechanism suitable for 90% of everyday use cases\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBLockedObject< T >\fP"
.br
.RI "Provides a minimal lock‑protected wrapper around a value of type \fIT\fP  using a caller‑supplied lock implementation\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBMutexLock\fP"
.br
.RI "A thin wrapper around operating‑system synchronization primitives (Mutex and EventWaitHandle)\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBRCUObject< T >\fP"
.br
.RI "Represents a minimal Read-Copy-Update (RCU) container that provides lock-free read access and exclusive write access to a protected value\&. Reader activity is tracked through an \fBEpoch\fP instance, while writers are synchronized using an \fBILock\fP\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBSafeCounter\fP"
.br
.RI "Provides a lightweight atomic counter with increment, decrement and assignment\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBScopedLock< T, TLOCK >\fP"
.br
.RI "Provides an RAII-style scoped lock for any \fBILock\fP implementation and exposes a snapshot of a protected value\&. The lock is acquired in the constructor and automatically released when the instance is disposed\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBScopedLock< TLOCK >\fP"
.br
.RI "Provides a scoped lock mechanism for an existing \fBILock\fP instance\&. Upon construction, the lock is acquired using the specified timeout\&. When the scope ends, \fBDispose\fP releases the lock\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBScopedUnlock< TLOCK >\fP"
.br
.RI "Provides a scoped unlock mechanism for an existing \fBILock\fP instance\&. Upon construction, the lock is immediately released\&. When the scope ends, \fBDispose\fP reacquires the lock using the specified timeout\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBSmallIndex\fP"
.br
.RI "Represents a thread-safe index counter that can be incremented, decremented, and compared atomically\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBSpinlock\fP"
.br
.RI "Provides a thin wrapper around System\&.Threading\&.SpinLock to expose a busy‑wait mutual exclusion primitive through the \fBISpinlock<T>\fP interface\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBThreadEx\fP"
.br
.RI "Provides a managed thread wrapper with event‑based control mechanisms\&. \fBThreadEx\fP supports starting, stopping, pausing, resuming, joining, and sending custom events to the running thread\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBUniqueEpoch\fP"
.br
.RI "Provides an RAII-style scoped reader epoch for RCU-based objects\&. The epoch is incremented when the instance is created and decremented when the instance is disposed\&. This guarantees deterministic reader tracking even in the presence of exceptions\&. "
