.SS "enum \fBSystemEx\&.Threading\&.ThreadInvokeMessage\fP"

.PP
Defines the types of invoke messages that can be delivered to a \fBLightThread\fP during an active invoke context\&. Each message type represents a different category of thread‑side operation, ranging from general data delivery to coroutine scheduling and stack transfer\&. 
.PP
\fBEnumerator\fP
.in +1c
.TP
\f(BIMessage \fP
A general-purpose message containing arbitrary external or internal data for the thread\&. 
.br
 Typical use cases include input events (e\&.g\&., mouse or device data), sensor updates, or any other runtime information the thread may consume\&. 
.TP
\f(BIPropertie \fP
A property or configuration update for the thread\&. 
.br
 Used to modify thread-specific settings, behavior flags, or other control parameters\&. 
.TP
\f(BICoRoutine \fP
A coroutine scheduling request\&. 
.br
 The message payload contains the entry point for a new coroutine that the thread should initialize and execute in future cycles\&. 
.TP
\f(BIStack \fP
A stack transfer message used by coroutine execution\&. 
.br
 Provides a stack of objects that represents coroutine state, arguments, or continuation data for internal coroutine processing\&. 
